ior to eating out at a restaurant . she can also use zofran if needed . however , i have encouraged her to reduce greasy and fatty foods and alcohol consumption . i have asked her to follow up in one month by emailing over mychart regarding any side effects and issues , or issues with elavil or if adjustments are needed .\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ **1. Subjective:**\n**Chief Complaint (CC):**\nMs. Brittany Edwards, a 32-year-old female, presents for a follow-up visit for Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) with functional abdominal pain and nausea.\n\n**History of Present Illness (HPI):**\nMs. Edwards is a pleasant, 32-year-old female who was initially seen in August 2019 with flares of abdominal pain and was diagnosed with IBS. She was prescribed Bentyl 20 mg for intestinal cramping and instructed to start a low-dose fiber supplement, such as Citrucel, daily, probiotics to help with gas and bloating, and to stop Reglan and use Zofran as needed. Neuromodulators like Elavil and Buspar were discussed but not started.\n\n**Review of Systems (ROS):**\n- **Gastrointestinal (GI):** Reports frequent diarrhea, nausea, and abdominal pain.\n- **Psychiatric:** No history of depression or anxiety.\n\n**2. Objective:**\n**Physical Exam:**\n- **General:** Alert and cooperative, appears stated age.\n- **Cardiovascular:** Regular rate and rhythm.\n- **Respiratory:** Lungs clear to auscultation bilaterally.\n- **Abdominal:** Soft, non-tender, no masses or organomegaly, active bowel sounds present.\n\n**Investigations:**\n- **Labs:** No relevant labs ordered.\n\n**3. Assessment:**\n- **Diagnosis:** Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) with functional abdominal pain and nausea.\n\n**4. Plan:**\n- **Medications:**\n  - **Bentyl:** Prescribed for intestinal cramping.\n  - **Zofran:** Prescribed for nausea as needed.\n  - **Elavil:** Initiated at 25 mg at bedtime for IBS.\n\n**Patient Education:**\n- Discussed the importance of dietary and lifestyle modifications, including reducing greasy and fatty foods, sugary drinks, and alcohol consumption.\n- Recommended Citrucel 2 tablets daily for regularity.\n- Encouraged her to use Bentyl 20 mg 30-45 minutes before eating out at restaurants.\n- Discussed the importance of water intake and avoiding sodas.\n- Discussed the potential side effects of Elavil and the importance of regular follow-up.\n\n**Follow-up:**\n- Follow-up in one month via email through MyChart to monitor the effectiveness of Elavil and to assess any side effects.\n\n**Patient Agreement:**\nMs. Edwards understands and agrees with the recommended treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ \n  HPC: 1898\n  PC: \n  Sx: \n  PMHx: \n  SHx: \n  DHx: \n  FHx: \n  MHx: \n  DX: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \n  PLAN: \n  IMP: \n  ASMT: \