illes tendon. No fever, chills, or weight loss.\n- **Physical Examination:** The patient appears in no acute distress. The right Achilles tendon shows tenderness to palpation, and the patient reports pain with passive ankle dorsiflexion.\n\n**4. Plan:**\n- **Medication:** Ibuprofen 200 mg, 3 tablets orally every 6 hours as needed for pain and inflammation.\n- **Referrals:** Referral to physical therapy for 2 sessions to address strength and stretching exercises.\n- **Follow-up:** Follow-up in 7-10 days to review progress and reassess.\n- **Education:** The patient was educated on the importance of proper stretching and strengthening exercises to alleviate pain and inflammation. Discussed the need to stop training for a week or two to allow the Achilles tendon to heal.\n- **Instructions:** The patient was advised to take Ibuprofen as prescribed and to follow up in 7-10 days. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ HPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\nHPC: 5/10\n